CM_ BO_ 115 "PLACEHOLDER: signals and payload length are not defined; zero DLC is a drafting marker, not an approved transmit layout. Four SMB status bitmaps: widths and bit definitions pending.";
CM_ BO_ 116 "Cyclic BPS report mirroring the BPSCommand payload: Mode, MPPTChargeScheme, VoltageOverrideMask, and TemperatureOverrideMask. Reports command values held by BPS; does not imply successful application or act as a per-request acknowledgement. Cyclic report every 1000 ms.";
CM_ SG_ 116 TemperatureOverrideMask "Bit 0 selects temperature 1; bit 31 selects temperature 32. Set bit requests the corresponding override.";
CM_ SG_ 116 VoltageOverrideMask "Bit 0 selects tap 1; bit 31 selects tap 32. Set bit requests the corresponding override.";
CM_ SG_ 116 MPPTChargeScheme "MPPTChargeScheme";
CM_ SG_ 116 Mode "Mode";
CM_ BO_ 117 "Latch once when BPS transitions from no active faults to any active fault, before opening contactors where possible. Send immediately, then every 1000 ms only while any BPS fault remains active. Keep captured samples frozen; never replace them with post-trip zeros. Rearm after all faults clear. Triggered transmission with a 1000 ms active-fault repeat interval; no transmission outside the send condition. Fault bits record the first fault state. BatteryCurrent preserves the live message scaling. CurrentSampleAgeMs describes sampling latency; this is not a guaranteed instantaneous peak measurement.";
CM_ SG_ 117 SampleAgeMs "Age in milliseconds of the oldest continuous sensor sample included in this frame when assembled; saturates at 65535. Age must advance for cached samples. In a fault snapshot, freeze age at fault detection; per-channel captured ages, if present, remain authoritative for individual trip records.";
CM_ SG_ 117 BatteryCurrent "BatteryCurrent";
CM_ SG_ 117 CaptureTimeMs "BPS monotonic uptime at fault detection, wraps at 2^32 ms; independent of legacy TimestampSync ticks.";
CM_ SG_ 117 CurrentValid "1 only if BatteryCurrent was sampled successfully before capture; otherwise ignore BatteryCurrent and CurrentSampleAgeMs.";
