CM_ BO_ 144 "LVC warnings and discrete states only; no fault bits. HSS warnings describe the single BPS feed HSS. BPSLVBlownFuse uses separate hardware monitoring; the PDU feed is separate.";
CM_ SG_ 144 BPSLVEnabled "Requested enable state of BPS HSS output channel 1; not proof of output voltage.";
CM_ SG_ 144 DCDCEnabled "DC-DC enable state.";
CM_ SG_ 144 WarningBPSLVBlownFuse "Separate hardware fuse monitor on the BPS feed; independent of HSS open-load diagnostics.";
CM_ SG_ 144 WarningNoDCDCOutput "DC-DC output unavailable.";
CM_ SG_ 144 WarningHSSWatchdog "LVC BPS HSS chip diagnostic: Watchdog. SPIError includes MCU-detected SPI/frame/CRC failures.";
CM_ SG_ 144 WarningHSSSPIError "LVC BPS HSS chip diagnostic: SPIError. SPIError includes MCU-detected SPI/frame/CRC failures.";
CM_ SG_ 144 WarningHSSVBBUndervoltage "LVC BPS HSS chip diagnostic: VBBUndervoltage. SPIError includes MCU-detected SPI/frame/CRC failures.";
CM_ SG_ 144 WarningHSSShortToBattery "BPS HSS output ShortToBattery warning; overtemperature combines absolute and relative thermal shutdown.";
CM_ SG_ 144 WarningHSSOpenLoad "BPS HSS output OpenLoad warning; overtemperature combines absolute and relative thermal shutdown.";
CM_ SG_ 144 WarningHSSOverTemperature "BPS HSS output OverTemperature warning; overtemperature combines absolute and relative thermal shutdown.";
CM_ SG_ 144 WarningHSSI2T "BPS HSS output I2T warning; overtemperature combines absolute and relative thermal shutdown.";
CM_ SG_ 144 WarningHSSOverCurrent "BPS HSS output OverCurrent warning; overtemperature combines absolute and relative thermal shutdown.";
CM_ BO_ 145 "10 Hz measured LV currents. BPSLVCurrent belongs to the single populated HSS output; no fictitious PDU HSS channel is reported.";
CM_ SG_ 145 SampleAgeMs "Age in milliseconds of the oldest continuous sensor sample included in this frame when assembled; saturates at 65535. Age must advance for cached samples. In a fault snapshot, freeze age at fault detection; per-channel captured ages, if present, remain authoritative for individual trip records.";
CM_ SG_ 145 BPSLVCurrent "Measured BPSLVCurrent.";
CM_ SG_ 145 TotalOutputCurrent "Measured TotalOutputCurrent. Independently measured total output, not a sum of HSS channels. The PDU feed is included only through this actual total measurement.";
CM_ SG_ 145 LVBCurrent "Measured LVBCurrent. Positive = battery discharge into LV supply; negative = battery charging.";
CM_ SG_ 145 DCDCCurrent "Measured DCDCCurrent.";
CM_ BO_ 146 "2 Hz LV voltage telemetry. HSS-derived BPSLVVoltage can stop updating when ADC conversion is suspended; consult sample age and chip diagnostics.";
CM_ SG_ 146 SampleAgeMs "Age in milliseconds of the oldest continuous sensor sample included in this frame when assembled; saturates at 65535. Age must advance for cached samples. In a fault snapshot, freeze age at fault detection; per-channel captured ages, if present, remain authoritative for individual trip records.";
CM_ SG_ 146 BPSLVVoltage "Measured BPSLVVoltage; zero is representable to expose a powered-off output.";
CM_ SG_ 146 PowerSupplyVoltage "Measured PowerSupplyVoltage; zero is representable to expose a powered-off output.";
CM_ SG_ 146 LVBVoltage "Measured LVBVoltage; zero is representable to expose a powered-off output.";
CM_ SG_ 146 DCDCVoltage "Measured DCDCVoltage; zero is representable to expose a powered-off output.";
CM_ BO_ 147 "1 Hz BPS HSS FET temperature; temperature conversions can be suspended in applicable I2T modes; consult sample age and chip diagnostics.";
CM_ SG_ 147 SampleAgeMs "Age in milliseconds of the oldest continuous sensor sample included in this frame when assembled; saturates at 65535. Age must advance for cached samples. In a fault snapshot, freeze age at fault detection; per-channel captured ages, if present, remain authoritative for individual trip records.";
CM_ SG_ 147 BPSFETTemperature "Internal temperature of the BPS channel power FET, not load/ambient temperature.";
CM_ BO_ 148 "Latch the first overcurrent or I2T trip per output until an explicit firmware fault-reset action. Freeze the last pre-trip current, its age at detection and the sending board monotonic uptime at detection. Reading diagnostic registers does not clear the telemetry latch. Send immediately on a new trip, then every 1000 ms while a trip remains latched. Never overwrite a captured current with post-shutdown zero. No snapshot/event identifier is sent. Capture time resets on board reboot. This records a sampled current, not a guaranteed instantaneous analog peak.";
CM_ SG_ 148 SampleAgeMs "Age in milliseconds of the oldest continuous sensor sample included in this frame when assembled; saturates at 65535. Age must advance for cached samples. In a fault snapshot, freeze age at fault detection; per-channel captured ages, if present, remain authoritative for individual trip records.";
CM_ SG_ 148 TripCurrent "Captured current; independent record per output; saturation marks a lower bound.";
CM_ SG_ 148 CaptureTimeMs "Board uptime at the first latched trip; wraps at 2^32 ms. Interpret only while a trip flag is set.";
CM_ SG_ 148 TripCurrentSaturated "1 if the captured current is clipped or the sensing path was saturated; the current is then a lower bound, not an exact peak.";
CM_ SG_ 148 FaultI2T "Latched I2T trip for BPS feed.";
CM_ SG_ 148 FaultOverCurrent "Latched OverCurrent trip for BPS feed.";
