CM_ BO_ 164 "Latch the first overcurrent or I2T trip per output until an explicit firmware fault-reset action. Freeze the last pre-trip current, its age at detection and the sending board monotonic uptime at detection. Reading diagnostic registers does not clear the telemetry latch. Send immediately on a new trip, then every 1000 ms while a trip remains latched. Never overwrite a captured current with post-shutdown zero. No snapshot/event identifier is sent. Capture time resets on board reboot. This records a sampled current, not a guaranteed instantaneous analog peak. Each output retains its own first trip; a later trip on another channel never replaces existing channel records.";
CM_ SG_ 164 SampleAgeMs "Age in milliseconds of the oldest continuous sensor sample included in this frame when assembled; saturates at 65535. Age must advance for cached samples. In a fault snapshot, freeze age at fault detection; per-channel captured ages, if present, remain authoritative for individual trip records.";
CM_ SG_ 164 TripCurrent6 "Captured current; independent record per output; saturation marks a lower bound.";
CM_ SG_ 164 CurrentSampleAgeMs6 "Age of the saved current sample when this channel tripped; frozen, saturates at 65535 ms.";
CM_ SG_ 164 CaptureTimeMs6 "Board uptime at the first latched trip; wraps at 2^32 ms. Interpret only while a trip flag is set.";
CM_ SG_ 164 TripCurrent5 "Captured current; independent record per output; saturation marks a lower bound.";
